      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Form the team and establish goals"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 2. Determine roles and responsibilities; develop a common understanding of the health programme's needs and goals; understand programme operations across levels of the health system."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_FormTeam",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_FormTeam",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_linkenterprisearchitecture",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Link to the enterprise architecture"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 6. Assess the digital health enterprise architecture, identify the common and enabling components and shared services that make up the digital health platform, and link the investment to both."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_LinkEnterpriseArchitecture",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_LinkEnterpriseArchitecture",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_mapcurrentstate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Map the current state and confirm bottlenecks"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 3.1. Determine the health programme processes to target, map their workflows, identify and confirm bottlenecks. Then 3.2, a root cause analysis. This is where DIIG builds on CRDM, and it says so: \"This process builds on the Public Health Informatics Institute's Collaborative Requirements Development Methodology (CRDM)\". Its three areas of concentration are business process analysis, business process redesign and requirements definition — two of which name diagrams this platform already executes. They are parallel tracks, not a composite: pick one per decision and name it."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_MapCurrentState",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_MapCurrentState",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_monitorandusedata",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Monitor, and use data effectively"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 8. Establish a logic model, plan the monitoring and evaluation, establish a culture of data use, and manage adaptively — using the data to optimize the interventions rather than only to report on them. The full treatment of this chapter is a separate publication in this library, `9789241511766-eng`, Monitoring and Evaluating Digital Health Interventions. It is a parallel track, not a sub-step: do not blend the two."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_MonitorAndUseData",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_MonitorAndUseData",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_planimplementation",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Plan the implementation"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 5. Infrastructure; legislation, policy and compliance, including data management, privacy and security, and the regulation of new technologies; leadership and governance, including external partnerships; workforce and training; services and applications."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_PlanImplementation",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_PlanImplementation",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_prioritizebottlenecks",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Prioritize, and map to health system challenges"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapters 3.3 and 3.4. Prioritize the bottlenecks, then map the programme-specific ones onto the generic health system challenges. THE ARITHMETIC IS REFUSED HERE. DIIG Table 3.3.1 asks three questions, each scored 1-3 — how much impact does this bottleneck have on the process, what is the likelihood of overcoming it, is it important to a wide range of stakeholders — and sums them into a Score and a Prioritized Ranking. The three criteria are adopted whole; the total is not. Record each criterion's answer AND its reason, and order by argument. A ranked list reads as evidence in a way three stated judgements do not, and the weights were invented."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_PrioritizeBottlenecks",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_PrioritizeBottlenecks",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_diig.a_valueproposition",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Make the value proposition and set next steps"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "DIIG Chapter 9. The case made to whoever pays, and what follows. Scaling up is a different method and a different publication — `9789241509510-eng`, The MAPS Toolkit — which begins where this implementation ends."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_ValueProposition",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/methodologies/processes/diig-investment-path.bpmn#A_ValueProposition",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2componenteditreview.call_review",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review the staged component [content-review]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "cat-harness's generic review, not a copy of it: classify what changed, review it, and record the decision as a qa-review/v1 QaReview whose subject is the component and whose Decision carries the reviewing role. The reviewer reads the staged page and the before/after; for a figure or table, the visual-diff picture and its changed-pixel count; for a form, the wireframe (wireframe-design-review; at L3 its Questionnaire follows fhir-questionnaire-wireframe). What to judge per component is the skill l2-component-edit-review's column \"the reviewer judges\"."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Review",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn#Call_Review",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2componenteditreview.task_check",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Run the component's checker [content-validate · content-test]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The mechanical checks for this component, before anyone is asked (skill l2-component-edit-review, column \"checker\"): BPMN imports in bpmn-js with no warnings and its lanes map to personas (dak-swimlanes.ts); DMN loads, its decisions are reachable (artefact-reachability, audit:reachability) and its test cases run (content-test); the data dictionary's ids are unique and its references and terminology bindings resolve (check-dak-annexes.ts); personas, scenarios and requirements each trace to an L1 recommendation (recommendation-extraction's implementedBy edges). Findings travel with the review request; a failing check does not stop the hand-on, it is a finding the reviewer sees."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Check",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn#Task_Check",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2componenteditreview.task_edit",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Edit the component [l2-component-edit-review]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Create or change the component with the authoring skill the call names (l2-dak-authoring, bpmn-authoring, dmn-authoring or terminology-management), one component per pass. On rework, apply the review's findings; a fix the reviewer wrote in an AuditNote is applied as given. An adapted component is edited against its pinned upstream, so the before side of the diff is that upstream, not an empty file."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Edit",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn#Task_Edit",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2componenteditreview.task_renderstage",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Render, stage, before/after [before-after-preview · feature-staging]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Render the component the way its reviewer reads it (column \"renderer and diff\"): the BPMN diagram (render:bpmn) with a visual-diff picture; the DMN decision table (smart-base-transform.py dmn2html) with each rule's L1 citation; the data dictionary's term diff (dak-data-dictionary-diff.ts) and the chosen wireframe of each form; personas, scenarios and requirements as a prose diff. Commit to the feature branch so it is staged as STAGING/<slug>/ on the platform's just-the-docs site (for smart-base, a folio-assistant staging re-pin, never the IG's /deploy), and make the before/after preview here, in the producing lane, so it exists when review starts."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RenderStage",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn#Task_RenderStage",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2componenteditreview.task_reopenupstream",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Reopen upstream, flag derived assets [todo-manager]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "File a bean against the stage that chose the rejected source or dependency (check for an existing bean first), and mark every asset derived from this component adjudication: rejected-upstream on its wasDerivedFrom edge. Nothing is deleted ahead of time: the re-derivation may come out the same."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_ReopenUpstream",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn#Task_ReopenUpstream",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2componenteditreview.task_requestreview",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Ask for review with staging deep links [staging-review]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Ask the person in the reviewing role, following staging-review's deep-link rule: one deep link per changed page and anchor on STAGING/<slug>/, each beside the same page on main as before (or \"new page\"), the pages taken from the change (rendered-impact) rather than chosen; no preview yet is said, not hidden. The request leads with what changed in prose, then the links, the before/after and the checker's findings, and puts its question in interaction-modality's form. Where it goes is a judgement, and more than one place may be right: this conversation, the GitHub issue the work came from, the pull request; each place carries the same links. A comment tagged on the PR becomes a review-comment todo (review-comments)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RequestReview",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn#Task_RequestReview",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
