      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Decision logic · DMN tables [dmn-authoring]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Author the decision and scheduling logic as DMN tables, within the FEEL subset the interpreter implements (any, literals, comparisons, one-of). Ranges, not() and function calls are refused at load, so write inside the subset. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the DMN inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: load, reachability, test cases; renderer: dmn2html table before/after, each rule beside its L1 citation; reviewer: clinical SME)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Dmn",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn#Task_Dmn",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2dak.task_indicators",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Indicators and requirements [l2-dak-authoring]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Author the component's indicators and its functional and non-functional requirements. These are the DAK's requirements, distinct from skills/requirements/*.json, which are this harness's own conformance obligations. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the indicators-and-requirements inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: each names the persona and process it serves and traces to L1; renderer: prose diff; reviewer: business analyst with the programme manager)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Indicators",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn#Task_Indicators",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2dak.task_l1library",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Build the L1 library from Component 1 [dak-l1-library]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Ingest the DAK into the library; it is L2, so it gets no L1 graph. Read Component 1 §1.2 for the sources it draws on (extract-dak-l1-references.ts --context-only), then fetch each L1 source on its own — fetch-dspace-item.ts for an IRIS handle, fetch-who-publication.ts for a who.int item page — and ingest it. Record whether each is L1 on its intake (declared > context > inferred; --record-context writes §1.2's context). For each L1 source, run l1-specialise.ts: its publication, sections and elements as specialisations of its library nodes, since the library is upstream of L1. Validate with the smart-base Zod validator. Fidelity — does each citation name the source it resolves to — and a cited edition older than the one fetched are left to a person, never passed automatically."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_L1Library",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn#Task_L1Library",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2dak.task_personas",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Personas and scenarios [l2-dak-authoring]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Author the DAK's personas and the user journeys (scenarios) they appear in, then have them reviewed: calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the personas-and-scenarios inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: dak-swimlanes.ts and traceability to L1 recommendations; renderer: the persona card and a prose diff; reviewer: clinical SME). These are the DAK's own actors, not this harness's scenarios/roles.json — the two vocabularies must not be conflated."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Personas",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn#Task_Personas",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2dak.task_scopedak",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Scope the DAK [content-plan]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Enumerate the processes, decisions and data elements the guideline implies; identify the actors."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_ScopeDak",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn#Task_ScopeDak",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2dak.task_seedbeans",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Seed the work plan [todo-manager]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Turn the scope into beans on the shared work plan — one per DAK component, since a DAK is completed component by component. beans create is not idempotent: check for an existing bean before every create, or a re-run duplicates the plan."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_SeedBeans",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn#Task_SeedBeans",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2dak.task_smevalidate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Clinical validation [content-review]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Ground truth: does the DAK say what the guideline says? This is the whole-DAK reading, across components: whether the personas, processes, decisions, data elements and indicators tell one consistent story. Each component has already had its own review, forking off inside its track (Process_L2ComponentEditReview, skill l2-component-edit-review), so this step does not repeat those per-component reviews."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_SmeValidate",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn#Task_SmeValidate",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_l2dak.task_terminology",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/smart-base/0.1.0/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Terminology bindings [terminology-management]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "ICD-11, SNOMED CT, LOINC bindings — governed separately from the artifacts that cite them. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the terminology inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: bindings resolve and unmappedConcepts is reported; renderer: the term diff on the code columns; reviewer: a terminologist other than the one who bound it)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Terminology",
      "dcterms:source": "smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn#Task_Terminology",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
